ns. Evidence indicates that TCAs exert quinidine-like membrane-stabilizing effects that contribute to conduction abnormalities and pro-arrhythmic potential, especially at elevated plasma concentrations. These findings support caution in prescribing TCAs to individuals with cardiovascular disease [Data: Relationships (8064, 8078); Entities (15563, 15940)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Contraindication in cardiovascular disease (CVD) patients\",\n            \"explanation\": \"三环类抗抑郁药 are explicitly contraindicated for CVD患者 due to their potential to prolong the QT interval and increase the risk of Torsades de Pointes (TdP), particularly when combined with other QT-prolonging agents. Clinical guidance notes that drugs like citalopram and venlafaxine also pose QT risks, but TCAs are flagged as high-risk due to their sodium channel blockade and negative inotropic effects. This contraindication reflects a well-documented safety concern that limits their use in a significant patient population with comorbid depression and heart disease [Data: Relationships (5398); Entities (14307)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Neuropsychiatric adverse reaction: 情绪降低\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Paradoxically, while TCAs are used to treat depression, they are associated with 情绪降低 (mood lowering) as an adverse reaction, particularly at high plasma concentrations (>450 μg/L). This central nervous system toxicity may manifest alongside other neurological symptoms such as confusion, hallucinations, seizures, and coma. The occurrence of mood worsening highlights the narrow therapeutic window of TCAs and the importance of therapeutic drug monitoring to avoid toxic levels [Data: Relationships (8083); Entities (16136)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"High-risk drug–drug interactions with SSRIs and MAOIs\",\n            \"explanation\": \"三环类抗抑郁药 exhibit clinically significant interactions with SSRIs (e.g., 氟西汀) and MAO inhibitors. Co-administration with SSRIs like fluoxetine or sertraline can increase TCA plasma concentrations by 58% to 375%, raising the risk of toxicity. Additionally, combining TCAs with MAOIs may precipitate hypertensive crises, serotonin syndrome, or even cardiac arrest. Guidelines recommend a minimum 14-day washout period between these drug classes. These interactions necessitate careful medication reconciliation and dose adjustments [Data: Relationships (31844, 26520, 26979)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Pharmacological interaction with antihypertensives like 胍乙啶\",\n            \"explanation\": \"多虑平 (doxepin), a TCA, interacts with 胍乙啶, an antihypertensive agent, by interfering with norepinephrine reuptake and storage. Although doxepin’s effect is weaker than other TCAs, co-administration with guanethidine or similar agents (e.g., reserpine) can lead to norepinephrine depletion in cardiac tissue, potentially causing bradycardia or cardiac arrest. This antagonism reduces the antihypertensive efficacy of guanethidine and poses life-threatening cardiovascular risks, warranting avoidance of concurrent use [Data: Relationships (35182)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Metabolic and biochemical impact on monoamine systems\",\n            \"explanation\": \"三环类抗抑郁药 significantly affect 单胺类 (monoamines) by inhibiting their reuptake and altering metabolism in both in vitro and in vivo settings. This mechanism underlies their antidepressant efficacy but also contributes to side effects and interactions. Unlike monoamine oxidase inhibitors (MAOIs), which only partially inhibit monoamine metabolism, TCAs like 丙咪嗪 and 氯丙咪嗪 produce more pronounced effects on monoamine availability. This biochemical activity explains both therapeutic outcomes and risks such as serotonin syndrome when combined with other serotonergic agents [Data: Relationships (187); Entities (13407)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Inclusion of diverse TCA-specific agents in the community\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The community includes several specific tricyclic antidepressants—去甲丙咪嗪, 多虑平, 氯丙咪嗪, 去郁敏, 普鲁替林, and 去甲替林—each with documented roles within the TCA class. These drugs share core pharmacological properties but may differ in potency, side effect profiles, and interaction potentials. For instance, 去甲替林 is noted for its interaction with SSRIs, while 氯丙咪嗪 is uniquely associated with 肺毒性 (pulmonary toxicity). This diversity illustrates the heterogeneity within the TCA class and the need for individualized risk assessment [Data: Entities (4079, 4849, 6293, 4101, 5797, 4086); Relationships (13090, 26520)].\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"rating\": 7.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The community poses a high clinical impact due to the serious cardiovascular and neurological risks of tricyclic antidepressants, significant drug–drug interactions, and contraindications in vulnerable populations like CVD patients.\"\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "provider_specific_fields": {"refusal": null}}, "provider_specific_fields": {}}], "created": 1782126679, "model": "qwen3-max", "object": "chat.completion", "moderation": null, "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1652, "prompt_tokens": 7035, "total_tokens": 8687, "completion_tokens_details": null, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 1280}}, "formatted_response": null, "content": "{\n    \"title\": \"三环类抗抑郁药 and Associated Drugs, Indications, and Risks\",\n    \"summary\": \"This community centers on the drug class '三环类抗抑郁药' (tricyclic antidepressants, TCAs), which is linked to multiple specific drugs (e.g., 去甲丙咪嗪, 多虑平, 氯丙咪嗪), a related drug class (三环抗抑郁药物), medical indications (e.g., 单相抑郁症), contraindicated populations (CVD患者), adverse reactions (e.g., 出血性卒中, 心室内传导延长, 情绪降低), and pharmacological 